SUMMARY: Point of View Talk with Ecologist Dawn Bazely and Screening of B
 rakfesten / La Grande Bouffe
DESCRIPTION:We are pleased to invite you to a special screening and talk 
 next Tuesday\, June 2\, 6-7:30PM at The Goldfarb Gallery featuring York B
 iology Professor Dawn Bazely.\n\nResponding to Anne Duk Hee Jordan: World
 s Away\, Professor Bazely will offer insights through the lens of ecology
 \, with a focus on plant–animal relationships and interdependence within 
 natural systems.\n\nThe program includes a screening of Brakfesten / La G
 rande Bouffe (2022–23)\, a film by Anne Duk Hee Jordan and Pauline Doutre
 luingne. Set in a Swedish forest threatened by Elm disease\, the film rev
 eals a fragile ecosystem and highlights the complex relationships among t
 he species that inhabit it.\n\nThe event will also be part of Toronto Cli
 mate Week.
CATEGORIES:Art-Show/Gallery-Event,Lecture/Book-Talk,Film
