UID:TKF/6755f42da02aaf1c2599e7ae/18969/29689920/0/0
DTSTART:20260614T000000Z
DTEND:20260614T020000Z
URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/18969/1781395200000
SUMMARY: Frequency: XUKASIA
DESCRIPTION:June 13 8pm $15-$20 adv $25 doors Join us for Frequency — a m
 onthly live music series at Worth Gallery. Frequency spotlights BIPOC mus
 icians of varying genres through intimate\, stripped-back shows. Celebrat
 ing sound\, connection\, and creative expression in Toronto's vibrant mus
 ic scene. Find your new favorite musician in your new favorite gallery. T
 his edition of Frequency features XUKASIA\, resident noisy music wallflow
 er. She'll be accompanied by experimental-techno producer/DJ Plastic Hear
 t Surgery. XUKASIA is a rapper and producer from Toronto\, creating exper
 imental abstract soundscapes within the genres of hip-hop\, hardcore elec
 tronic\, industrial\, punk\, ambient\, breakcore and synthwave house musi
 c. She's released two albums: "XONIKA!" and "XEONFLUXX!" Her lyrics are o
 ften raw and personal\, detailing her experiences with topics such as gen
 der identity\, mental health issues\, and manifesting positive energy. Sh
 e makes all her beats using FL Studio and an AKAI MPK midi controller. XU
 KASIA is also a show organizer\, putting on multiple series of showcases 
 like AFRONOIZE (Black queer showcase\, all genres) and ARMAGEDDON (queer 
 experimental showcase). Located in the lower gallery — down a flight of s
 tairs. For any other accessibility questions\, please feel free to reach 
 out to us.
