 , hotel manager Lisa Reisert (Rachel McAdams) is waiting to fly back home
  when she meets charming Jackson Rippner (Cillian Murphy) at check-in. Wh
 at begins as a charming meet-cute soon becomes a deadly descent into terr
 or as Lisa realizes she's inadvertently become part of an assassination p
 lot that also puts the life of her father Joe (Brian Cox) in danger.\n\nD
 irected by Wes Craven\, this 2005 thriller's box office take was nearly f
 our times its modest $26 million budget. It currently holds an 80% approv
 al rating on Rotten Tomatoes. Although Cillian Murphy doesn't rank his pe
 rformance in RED EYE as one of his best\, in 2021 he said\, "But\, listen
 \, if people love the movie then that's great. I'm pleased with that\," a
 dding in 2024 that he loves lead actress Rachel McAdams and they had fun 
 making the film: "It's a good B movie."\n\nFor the last screening in the 
 Cillian Me Softly series\, we have lots of fun surprises are in store\, i
 ncluding raffle prizes\, giveaways\, and much more. Follow IG:@socialjust
 icewendigo for details!\n\n$5.00 cash at the door or advance tickets thro
 ugh Eventbrite for $6.85\nPre-show: 7:30 pm\nFeature: 8 pm (85 minutes)
